      "expect": "owned",
      "why": "KNOWN IRREDUCIBLE LIMIT, pinned deliberately — this is NOT a shape we want to kill. A FORWARD-SLASH-SPELLED command line — on any host, since the gate is the path spelling and not the platform — that hands another program a CORRECTLY-NAMED macOS bundle executable path is byte-for-byte identical to a real bundle invocation (`/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome`), so no rule over the string can separate them; only the filesystem could. It is pinned as `owned` so that BOTH implementations keep agreeing about it and neither can widen or narrow the limit unnoticed. If a future change makes this `not-owned` WITHOUT losing the real bundle cases (`posix-mac-bundle-*`), that is an improvement — change this case then, deliberately. Mitigation today: it still requires the caller to pass our exact `--user-data-dir=<profile>`, which no ordinary vim/git/tar invocation carries."
